INT. MAIL SORTING DEPOT - 3 A.M.

Conveyor belts hum. Parcels tumble down chutes. Fluorescent light. No windows.

KARLOS (40s, supervisor, name tag) stands at a console. JIN (20s, forklift jacket) waits by a crate. MAREN (30s, uniform, ID lanyard) scans labels. DUBOIS (50s, suit, no tie) paces along the belt. OLD TIBBS (70s, janitor, mop bucket) wrings a rag.

KARLOS
Parcel 0447. It's due out at dawn.

DUBOIS
Open it.

JIN
Boss, that's federal.

DUBOIS
So am I.

Maren stops scanning. Tibbs goes still. The belt hums.

KARLOS
Nobody opens it until we know what's inside.

DUBOIS
I already know what's inside.

He pulls a pistol. Maren backs away. Jin raises both hands. Karlos steps forward.

KARLOS
Put that down.

DUBOIS
Open the crate.

Tibbs lunges with the mop. Dubois swings. The pistol fires into the ceiling. Sparks rain. Maren and Jin dive behind the belt. Karlos tackles Dubois. They crash onto the conveyor, rolling together toward a chute. Tibbs hits the emergency stop.

Everything goes silent. The gun skids across the floor. All five look at it.
